 # Business Rules — PegaFila
 
-Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements. Core domain issuance is implemented via `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (ticket into an active queue) and deterministic call-next via `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (three call modes + 3-ticket fairness); HTTP, Livewire, and billing remain future work.
+Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements. Core domain issuance is implemented via `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (ticket into an active queue) and deterministic call-next via `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (three call modes + 3-ticket fairness); the queue management page, the attendant serve panel and the members page are Livewire components (see "Queue UI" below); the totem API, TV screen and billing remain future work.
 
 ## MVP Scope
 
@@ -98,11 +98,13 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Queue lifecycle:** queues are managed by `App\Actions\CreateQueue` (owner/admin only, slug defaults to `Str::slug($name)`, unique per `(entity_id, slug)`) and `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` (owner/admin only, rename with the same uniqueness rule, toggle `is_active`). There is **no delete surface** — removal = `is_active = false`; tickets are history and remain intact, while `IssueTicket` / `CallNextTicket` reject inactive queues via `InactiveQueueException`.
 
-**Queue access:** employees operate only queues with a `queue_access` grant row (`permissions` JSON, MVP vocabulary `call` only via `App\Enums\QueuePermission`). Grants are managed by `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (owner/admin only, target membership and queue must share the entity, empty list revokes, audited to the `audit` channel). Owner/admin call without a grant row; non-members are denied everywhere. Authorization lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` (`create`/`update`/`manageAccess`/`call`) and is enforced server-side inside the domain actions, not only at future HTTP/Livewire callers.
+**Queue access:** employees operate only queues with a `queue_access` grant row (`permissions` JSON, MVP vocabulary `call` only via `App\Enums\QueuePermission`). Grants are managed by `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (owner/admin only, target membership and queue must share the entity, empty list revokes, audited to the `audit` channel). Owner/admin call without a grant row; non-members are denied everywhere. Authorization lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` (`create`/`update`/`manageAccess`/`call`) and is enforced server-side inside the domain actions, not only by the UI.
+
+**Queue UI (Livewire):** `App\Livewire\Entity\Queues` (`entity.queues`, `/e/{entity:slug}/queues`, owner/admin; employees get 403) creates, renames (slug re-derived from the name), deactivates/reactivates (confirmation modal) and manages per-queue `call` grants by calling `CreateQueue`, `UpdateQueue` and `SetQueueAccess`; domain validation errors are shown on the name field. `App\Livewire\Entity\Serve` (`entity.serve`, `/e/{entity:slug}/serve`, any member) lists the active queues the user may call (all for owner/admin, granted ones for employees), the first 30 waiting tickets in call order for the chosen mode, and `callNext()` through `CallNextTicket` (successful calls are rate limited to 10/min per user and entity). Every client-supplied queue or membership id is resolved scoped to the entity (`$entity->queues()->findOrFail()`), so foreign ids are a not-found and change nothing. The members page is split into a members tab and an invites tab.
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
